{"nodes": [{"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_layer", "label": "3js Three.js tile layer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All Three.js code is confined to one folder with a single public export surface (../3js) so the default 2D OpenCV view is untouched by anything in it."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_drawing_layer_only", "label": "Three.js is only a drawing layer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It does no room detection and never estimates vanishing points, camera angle, room size or tile size; it replays exactly what the 2D engine decided, so there is one source of geometric truth and the 3D view cannot drift from it."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_index_ts", "label": "3js/index.ts public exports", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetiles", "label": "threeTiles.ts core renderer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds the three.json types, loadThreeJob, projectionFromIntrinsics, surfaceGeometry, surfaceMaterial and TileLayerRenderer in one module so the camera, mesh and shader are built from the same recorded state."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetilelayer", "label": "ThreeTileLayer.tsx stacking component", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stacks photo, tiles and objects inside the image's own box, mirroring how the 2D composite puts furniture back over the tiles."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_projectionfromintrinsics", "label": "projectionFromIntrinsics", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Builds the Three.js camera from the engine's own focal_px and (cx, cy), evaluating pixel i at coordinate i exactly as the engine does, and converts the engine frame (x right, y down, z forward) to Three.js (x, -y, -z)."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_surfacematerial", "label": "surfaceMaterial tile shader", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reproduces the 2D engine's per-pixel steps in order - mask clip, grid, texture with wrap and height_stretch, constant-width grout faded below 1 px, lighting from the base image brightness, then tile opacity - so colour matches within 2 levels."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_per_pixel_grid", "label": "Per-pixel grid, not interpolated across the quad", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A wall reaching its vanishing line has a quad kilometres deep and float32 interpolation across it shifted the pattern, so u/v are computed per pixel with cos/sin taken from the CPU because GPU trigonometry is approximate."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_mask_only_clip", "label": "Mask is the only clip", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The surface is rasterized as a quad covering the whole image so every pixel is considered and only the white mask decides; verified at 0 pixels outside the mask and 0 white pixels undrawn."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_json", "label": "three.json render state record", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One per-surface record of camera intrinsics, plane and tile axes, meters_per_unit, visible quad in units and mm, grid rotation/offset, tile, grout, lighting and mask path - the single contract that lets the 3D layer replay a render without recomputing anything."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomconsistency", "label": "roomConsistency() validation gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checks every record against the render's room (same focal length and principal point, floor plane at the room's camera height, walls in room millimetres, tile size in mm) and refuses to draw with a stated reason rather than correcting with a scale of its own."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomgeometry", "label": "RoomGeometry canonical room (Phase 3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Floor and every wall of a render share one metric scale (the camera height), so per-surface meters_per_unit values already agree with each other and with room, and the 3D view adds no scale of its own."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_unit_is_metre", "label": "1 scene unit = 1 metre", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 600x1200 mm tile is 0.6 x 1.2 units and tiles are never resized, which is what makes quad edge lengths in the scene equal tile-grid lengths exactly."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_layer_py", "label": "three_layer.py record()", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Captures one rendered surface's state and is strictly read-only, never changing pixels, which is why the 2D output stayed byte-identical after the backend additions."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_floor_pipeline", "label": "floor_pipeline.py info['three']", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_wall_pipeline", "label": "wall_pipeline.py per-wall 'three' entry", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_render_py_three", "label": "backend render.py Rendered.three carrier", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries the per-surface records keyed floor or wall-<i>, which is the key scheme the frontend loader relies on."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_save_three", "label": "app.py _save_three and three_url", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes three.json plus three/<surface>.png and three/objects.png into the job folder and returns three_url from /generate; a surface rendered before three.json existed shows '3D view unavailable' until re-rendered."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_digit_package_constraint", "label": "Python cannot import a package starting with a digit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "That language constraint is why the Three.js layer lives in frontend/src/3js while its backend half stays under tiles_backend/perspective_engine instead of a matching 3js package."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_studio_page", "label": "pages/Studio.tsx 3D View button", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only consumer of the 3js folder; the button sits next to Compare and is enabled once a surface is tiled."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_parity", "label": "three_parity.py 3D-vs-2D verification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "3 frozen rooms, floor plus 12 walls, rotations 0/45/90/135, 60 renders and 10.7 M tile pixels: 100% of colours within 2 levels, zero mask violations, and 2D output byte-identical to before."}, {"id": "frontend_src_3js_readme_limits", "label": "3D view current limits", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The view is the photo's own camera with no free orbit yet; tile artwork is assumed opaque so a transparent tile blends over the photograph instead of the clean room; and any change of tile, size, grout or rotation still goes through the backend render first."}], "edges": [{"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_layer", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_index_ts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_layer", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_layer", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetilelayer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetiles", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_projectionfromintrinsics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetiles", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_surfacematerial", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_threetiles", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_json", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_projectionfromintrinsics", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_json", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_drawing_layer_only", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_layer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_per_pixel_grid", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_surfacematerial", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_mask_only_clip", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_surfacematerial", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomconsistency", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomgeometry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomconsistency", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_json", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_roomgeometry", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_unit_is_metre", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_layer_py", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_json", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_floor_pipeline", "target": "frontend_src_3js_readme_three_layer_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "frontend/src/3js/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "frontend_src_3js_readme_wall_pipeline", "target": "frontend_src_3